  "theorem_name": "PositiveTailDiagonalCoreBridgeAndAmbiguousBandNoGo",
  "declared_proposition": "Let Q_N be nested Galerkin compressions on a form core and write Q_N=A_(N,T_N)+R_(N,T_N), where R_(N,T_N) is positive semidefinite. If interval-certified lower bounds satisfy lambda_min(A_(N,T_N))>=-epsilon_N with epsilon_N tending to zero, then Q_N has the same vanishing negative defect and the TICKET-165 core-limit bridge proves nonnegativity of the limiting form. If an available tail norm has order (2N+1)log(T)/T, the diagonal choice T=N^3 makes that norm O(log N/N^2).",
  "mathematical_argument": "Positive semidefiniteness gives Q_N>=A_(N,T_N), hence the certified lower bound transfers without subtracting the tail. Core convergence then invokes the exact TICKET-165 limit theorem. Substituting T=N^3 into (2N+1)log(T)/T gives 3(2N+1)log(N)/N^3, which tends to zero. The tail budget alone does not decide an eigenvalue in [-B,0): the one-dimensional truncated value -B/2 completed by tails 0 and B has opposite full signs.",
